{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we start by analyzing the given geometric configuration. We know that the square \\(ABCD\\) has side length \\(s\\) and the circle centered at \\(E\\) has radius \\(r\\). The circle passes through \\(D\\) and \\(D\\) lies on \\(\\overline{BE}\\). Point \\(F\\) lies on the circle, on the same side of \\(\\overline{BE}\\) as \\(A\\), and segment \\(AF\\) is tangent to the circle. We are given that \\(AF = \\sqrt{9 + 5\\sqrt{2}}\\).\n\nFirst, let's place the square \\(ABCD\\) in the coordinate plane with \\(A = (0, s)\\), \\(B = (0, 0)\\), \\(C = (s, 0)\\), and \\(D = (s, s)\\). Since the circle passes through \\(D\\) and \\(D\\) lies on \\(\\overline{BE}\\), the center \\(E\\) of the circle must be on the line \\(y = x + s\\). Let \\(E = (a, a+s)\\). The radius \\(r\\) of the circle is the distance from \\(E\\) to \\(D\\), so we have:\n\\[\nr = \\sqrt{(a-s)^2 + (a+s-(a+s))^2} = \\sqrt{(a-s)^2} = |a-s|.\n\\]\nSince \\(r\\) is positive, we have \\(r = s - a\\) (assuming \\(a \\leq s\\)).\n\n","prefix_end":948,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1191,553,41018,279,2661,52484,6546,13,1205,1414,429,279,9334,17767,1867,6484,57758,702,3108,3084,17767,82,57758,323,279,12671,30188,518,17767,36,57758,702,10578,17767,81,59,568,576,12671,16211,1526,17767,35,57758,323,17767,35,57758,15448,389,1124,11520,1975,1056,90,11594,11035,568,5126,17767,37,57758,15448,389,279,12671,11,389,279,1852,3108,315,1124,11520,1975,1056,90,11594,11035,8,438,17767,32,59,701,323,10238,17767,8276,57758,374,68660,311,279,12671,13,1205,525,2661,429,17767,8276,284,1124,26888,90,24,488,220,20,59,26888,90,17,3417,59,3593,5338,11,1077,594,1992,279,9334,17767,1867,6484,57758,304,279,16184,11031,448,17767,32,284,320,15,11,274,10699,701,17767,33,284,320,15,11,220,15,10699,701,17767,34,284,320,82,11,220,15,10699,7